Bill delivery as an invoice line, company name on Generate Invoices, order screen rework (v0.102)

Delivery billed as a line item:
- Generate Invoices now bills an order's shipping/delivery cost as its
  own line on the invoice PDF ("DELIVERY", qty 1, VAT applied the same
  as a product line), instead of that cost only ever showing in the
  pre-invoice credit estimate and disappearing once the order's product
  lines are invoiced.
- Order.shippingInvoiced is a once-only guard so an order's delivery
  charge is billed on exactly one invoice, whichever generation run
  first touches that order, even if its lines end up split across more
  than one invoice run.
- Not applied to RMA credit notes - those credit returned goods, not the
  original outbound delivery charge.
- InvoiceLine.orderLine is now nullable (a shipping line has no product
  OrderLine behind it) with a new boolean "shipping" flag to tell it
  apart from a product line.
- CompanyService.creditUsed()'s bucket 2 (despatched, not yet invoiced)
  now also carries an order's shipping cost for as long as it stays
  unbilled, so it's counted in exactly one bucket as it moves from
  pre-despatch to despatched-but-unbilled to actually invoiced - closes
  the gap flagged in v0.101.

Generate Invoices:
- Each order's row now also shows its company name (previously only the
  group heading above it did), so a special requirement can be spotted
  without scrolling back up to check whose orders are being looked at.

Sales Activity / Order Edit:
- Order Lines now comes before the Despatch panel.
- The Despatch panel is now two columns: the existing release/despatch
  controls on the left, and a live Cost Breakdown on the right (Goods
  Net, Delivery, Total Net, Total Tax, Total Order) that recalculates
  immediately as order lines or the shipping cost are edited, using the
  linked company's VAT rate override or the Settings default - before
  the order is even saved.

Written and reviewed without a working compiler in this environment
(Maven Central/npm registry both blocked here) - please build and
smoke-test before relying on this, particularly Generate Invoices (the
new delivery line, and that shipping is billed exactly once per order)
and the reworked order screen's live cost breakdown.

